dropped the body
--
N5008 [upper.bound] + [range.access]: `std::ranges::upper_bound(array,
value)' -- the range overload of the niebloid on a built-in array, as
libc++'s <format> tables use it (`__estimated_width', `__get_property').
With libstdc++ 13 the result is right but bodies are dropped.  Round 163
fixed the range-access CPO `_Decay_copy::operator()' drop
(bits/iterator_concepts.h:971): it was instantiated with `_Tp = void'
from `__decay_copy(begin(__t))' over the poison pill, see
cpp20_reference_to_void_deduction_fails.  Still dropped: `declval<auto()>'
& co. (type_traits:2386).  Diagnosis (round 163): the range overload of
upper_bound is checked with `forward_range<const uint32_t *>'; its
`iterator_t<const uint32_t *>' = `decltype(__begin(declval<_Tp &>()))'
should be a substitution failure, but `_Begin::operator()' / `__begin'
(constexpr auto, `requires is_array_v<_Tp> || __member_begin<_Tp &> ||
__adl_begin<_Tp &>') is instantiated for the pointer anyway because the
parser's single-compound-requirement fast path (parse.cpp, "Try compound
requirement: { { expr } -> concept<type>; }") records only the method
name and no operand, and the typecheck treats the operand-less
`compound_requirement' as satisfied.  Removing the fast path makes the
`__member_begin' checks real, and then cpp20_ranges_basic (`arr |
views::take(3)') fails: `__t.begin()' on take_view / ref_view is
evaluated while the class is still being elaborated (view_interface CRTP
base members convert eagerly) and finds the namespace-scope CPO `begin'
instead ("'std::ranges::__cust::begin' is not static member of class
'struct take_view'"), so the whole adaptor pipeline is rejected.  The two
have to be fixed together.  With libc++ 18
(`--stdlib libc++') the call itself fails ("found no match for symbol
'operator()'" at __algorithm/ranges_upper_bound.h:54) and the unit is
rejected.  Audit residue items 4 and 10 (round 162); the `__estimated_width'
/ `__get_property' drops of every libc++ C++20 test are this shape.
